<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian I, Prince of Anhalt-Bernburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1568">1568</a>–1630</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian I, Prince of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernburg">Bernburg</a>, received Bernburg in the 1603 division of Anhalt. A Calvinist statesman in the service of the Palatinate, he was a chief organiser of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-union">Protestant Union</a> and the leading adviser of Frederick V in the Bohemian revolt. He commanded the army defeated at the White Mountain in 1620, and was later pardoned.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-i-prince-of-anhalt-bernburg.jpg" alt="Christian I, Prince of Anhalt-Bernburg" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circle of Michiel van Miereveld · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christian_I._von_Anhalt-Bernburg,_1609.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
